  "id": "Compound::DB00565 - Gene::1144",
  "verbalization": "Cisatracurium Besylate, a neuromuscular blocking agent, is linked to Chrnd through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cisatracurium Besylate, when bound to Chrnd, contributes to the pharmacological effects observed in neuromuscular blockade. This is supported by the fact that Cisatracurium Besylate is included in the category of Neuromuscular Nondepolarizing Blockade, which includes Vecuronium, a drug that binds to Chrnd. The relationship between Cisatracurium Besylate and Chrnd is further reinforced by the shared pathway through Nitrogen Molecular Entity and Nicotinic Antagonist, indicating a structural and functional connection at the molecular level. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Cisatracurium Besylate exerts its effects on Chrnd, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
